body:
What about `set_use_own_world_3d`? It seems to be similar and also have no check.

Following calls will still crash:
```gdscript
	get_viewport().world_3d = null
	get_viewport().own_world_3d = true
	get_viewport().own_world_3d = false
```
So it should have the same check.

```diff
diff --git a/scene/main/viewport.cpp b/scene/main/viewport.cpp
index 9f81349c4a..4412b9637c 100644
--- a/scene/main/viewport.cpp
+++ b/scene/main/viewport.cpp
@@ -4960,7 +4965,12 @@ void Viewport::set_use_own_world_3d(bool p_use_own_world_3d) {
        }

        if (is_inside_tree()) {
-               RenderingServer::get_singleton()->viewport_set_scenario(viewport, find_world_3d()->get_scenario());
+               const Ref<World3D> found_world = find_world_3d();
+               if (found_world.is_valid()) {
+                       RenderingServer::get_singleton()->viewport_set_scenario(viewport, found_world->get_scenario());
+               } else {
+                       RenderingServer::get_singleton()->viewport_set_scenario(viewport, RID());
+               }
        }
```
